message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Condición de conmutación e invariancia de orden en stacks dieléctricos bimateriales bajo polarización TM"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Roldán"
    given-names: "Nahuel Alejandro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6747-0756"
    affiliation: "Consejo Nacional de Investigaciones Científicas y Técnicas (CONICET)"
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-07"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/roldannahuelalejadro/thin-film-tmm-order-invariance"
abstract: >-
  A sufficient condition is derived under which the characteristic matrices
  of two dielectric materials commute independently of their thicknesses.
  For TM polarization, the resulting incidence angle makes the multilayer
  response depend only on accumulated phases and invariant under layer
  permutations, subject to the stated physical assumptions.
keywords:
  - thin films
  - transfer matrix method
  - matrix commutation
  - order invariance
  - TM polarization
